{% comment %}
  PartnerLoop attribution.

  Captures ?ref=<code> on any storefront page, stores it in a first-party cookie
  for the attribution window, reports the click through the app proxy, and
  copies the code onto the cart so it survives into the resulting order.

  This is an app embed block: it is OFF until the merchant enables it under
  Theme editor → App embeds. The app's dashboard warns when that hasn't happened.

  The block filename matters — it appears in the theme's settings_data.json as
  ".../blocks/partnerloop-tracking/<uuid>", which is how the app detects whether
  this embed is switched on. Renaming this file breaks that detection.
{% endcomment %}

<script
  src="{{ 'partnerloop-tracking.js' | asset_url }}"
  data-partnerloop-tracking
  data-proxy-base="/apps/partnerloop"
  data-window-days="30"
  defer
></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PartnerLoop tracking",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
